  ('q2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000158', 'e1000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 's2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001', 't2000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002', 'PYQ', '[UPPSC PCS 2014] Which one of the following Articles of the Indian Constitution empowers the Governor to promulgate Ordinances during recess of Legislature?', 'Article 123', 'Article 214', 'Article 213', 'Article 208', 'C', '{"why":"Article 213 empowers the Governor to promulgate ordinances when the state legislature is in recess. President''s power is under Article 123.","concept":"Article 213 - Ordinance Making Power of Governor","exam_perspective":"UPPSC regularly features direct factual articles, state geography, and applied physical science questions.","remember":"President = 123; Governor = 213 (digits swapped).","related_concept":"Article 123, DC Wadhwa case"}'::jsonb, 'moderate', 2014, 'UP Combined State / Upper Subordinate Exam GS-I', 'approved'),
